'''Andalus''', officially the '''Andalusian Republic''' ({{Langx|mxi|Repúblika Andalûça}}) and colloquially '''Andalusia''', is a {{W|sovereign state}} located mainly on the [[Andalusian Peninsula]] in the [[Eastern Mesogean]]. It shares land borders with <> and <> to the west, and a maritime border with [[Mauretania]] to the north. With an estimated population of 108 million in 2024, Andalus is the most populous state in the region, and the x-most populous in the world. With a total area of over 2.6 million sq mi Andalus is the x-largest nation in Illypnia, and the x-largest in the world.

In the early eighth century, the <> Kingdom was conquered by the [[Bayani Caliphate]], ushering in over 700 years of [[Al-Andalus|Muslim rule]]. During this period, <> became a major economic and intellectual center, with the city of [[Calatayud]] being among the largest and richest in Illypnia. Several [[Catharism|Catharist]] [[maritime republics]] states emerged in the southern periphery of the Andalusian Peninsula, chief among them [[Republic of Tartessia|Tartessia]], <> and <>. These republics later joined together in the [[Treaty of Tartessos]] to form the [[Andalusi League]]. Over the next seven centuries, an intermittent northward expansion of the League during the [[Andalusi–Mauretanian wars]] culminated with the League's conquest of the last Mauretanian polity, the [[Emirate of Albasarat]]. This precipitated the [[Andalusi rebellion]] of <>, which gave rise to a united and {{W|confederation|confederated}} Andalus and produced the [[Declaration of the Rights of Humanity]], which expresses the nation's ideals to this day. From the 16th until the late 20th century, the League ruled [[Andalusian Empire|one of the largest empires in history]], which was also the first {{W|List of largest empires|global empire}}; its immense cultural and linguistic legacy includes over 570 million [[<>]]s, making it the world's [[List of languages by number of native speakers|<>-most spoken native language]]. Andalus hosts the world's {{W|World Heritage Sites by country|largest}} number of {{W|UNESCO|TESCO}} {{W|World Heritage Sites}}. Inadequate economic policies, inequitable taxes and frequent wars left the Confederation in a precarious economic situation by the end of the 17th century, spurring the [[Age of Exploration]].

Andalus ranks among the highest in international measurements of {{W|government transparency}}, {{W|civil liberties}}, {{W|quality of life}}, {{W|social development}}, and {{W|education}}. As of 2022, Andalus is described as being highly democratic, with an {{W|open-source governance|open-source}}-system of governance that promotes universal {{W|participatory democracy|participation}}, beginning at the lowest level in it's {{W|administrative division}}s. This includes widespread support for a universalist [[Social protection in Andalus|social protection system]] aimed specifically at enhancing individual autonomy and promoting {{W|social mobility}}, a {{W|cooperative economics|cooperative}} system involving a tripartite arrangement where representatives of labour are integrated in government, and labour market policy is mediated by the government and a commitment to {{W|social ownership}} based on {{W|Mutualism (economic theory)|mutualism}}, with a large number of {{W|state-owned enterprises}} and state ownership in [[Essential industry (Andalus)|essential industries]]. As of 2020, Andalus ranks highly on the inequality-adjusted HDI and the {{W|Global Peace Index}} as well as being ranked in the top 10 on both the {{W|Social Progress Index}} and the {{W|World Happiness Report}}.

Andalus is a {{W|Developed country|highly developed country}}, and it's [[Economy of Andalus|economy]] is the world's fourth-[[Wikipedia:List of countries by GDP (nominal)|largest by nominal GDP]] and fourth-[[Wikipedia:List of countries by GDP (PPP)|largest by GDP (PPP)]]. Since the late 19th century, it has operated a mixed economy which synthesizes {{W|Mutualism (economic theory)|mutualist ideals}} with a [[W:Socialist-oriented market economy|socialist-oriented market economy]]. Its labor force is among the world's largest, most educated, and the [[Trade unions in Andalus|most unionized]]. The Andalusn government has followed a policy of {{W|military neutrality|international neutrality}} through {{W|non-alignment}} since to <>. Additionally, Andalus is a founding member of the [[Adonian Community]], the [[Mesogean Cooperation Council]], the [[Five Eyes]] and the [[Accelerationist International]]. Andalus is recognized [[W:Great power|great power]] in international affairs.

